          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Critically Acclaimed Works</strong><br>\nScorsese has directed a number of critically acclaimed films, including \"Taxi Driver\" (1976), \"Raging Bull\" (1980), and \"Goodfellas\" (1990). These films are celebrated for their powerful storytelling and have earned Scorsese a reputation as one of the greatest filmmakers of his time.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Diverse Genres and Documentaries</strong><br>\nWhile Scorsese is best known for his gangster films, he has explored various genres, including comedy, historical epic, and psychological thriller. He has also made significant contributions to documentary filmmaking with works on Bob Dylan, George Harrison, and the New York City music scene.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Contributions to Film Preservation</strong><br>\nScorsese is a staunch advocate for film preservation and has been involved in restoring and preserving classic films through his Film Foundation. His dedication to cinema history is reflected in his work and public advocacy.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
